data.content:
## What Breaks in .NET 11

In EF Core 11 (shipping with .NET 11), the **Cosmos DB provider removes sync-over-async support entirely**. The opt-in flag you configured in .NET 10 (`UseSyncOverAsync()` or the `CosmosOptionsExtension` workaround) no longer exists.

**All four methods will throw `InvalidOperationException`** at runtime with a message like:

> *"Synchronous operations are not supported by the Azure Cosmos DB provider. Use the corresponding async method instead."*

The affected calls:
| Method | Throws because |
|--------|---------------|
| `.ToList()` | Sync enumeration removed |
| `.First(...)` | Sync scalar operator removed |
| `.Count()` | Sync scalar operator removed |
| `.SaveChanges()` | Sync persist removed |

## The Fix

Convert to async throughout:

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

**Key points:**
- `Add()` remains synchronous (it only tracks in memory) — no change needed there.
- Callers must be updated to `await` these methods (async propagates up the call stack).
- If you have controllers calling these, mark the action methods `async Task<IActionResult>` as well.
